        "New tests are validated by confirming they fail on the prior commit and by mutation testing (11 of 12 caught initially)."
      ],
      "code": [
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/extractor/component.rs",
          "line": 73,
          "finding": "peel_expr reads through type instantiations, so `memo(List<Row>)` resolves to bare `List` and the type arguments are dropped without a Diagnostic."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/extractor/component.rs",
          "line": 598,
          "finding": "typeof_aliases runs a full-AST TypeNames visit on every file even when no `typeof` alias exists. It should run only when candidates exist."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/extractor/component.rs",
          "line": 626,
          "finding": "Counting declarations at any depth (type params, mapped keys) lets unrelated shadowing disable a valid typeof alias."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/extractor/component.rs",
          "line": 437,
          "finding": "`never` is classified as Returns::Neither, which maps to NotRenderable. It should be Unknown because `never` proves nothing about whether a call is a component."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/extractor/component.rs",
          "line": 156,
          "finding": "member() and combine return Unread/Unknown when one declaration is a setter or untyped, discarding decisive evidence from the other declarations."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/extractor/uses.rs",
          "line": 207,
          "finding": "renderable() accepts NoComponent evidence, so `(createElement as (t)=>string)(Foo)` counts Foo as rendered."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/extractor/evidence.rs",
          "line": 228,
          "finding": "Hook detection reads `peel(&it.callee).expr` directly and bypasses named(). This was deliberately kept, with the rationale that calling a hook is the evidence regardless of the asserted return type."
